<article class="env-proposition" id="1A8B">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/1A8B">Proposition <span data-tag="1A8B">5.5.3.6</span>.</a>presentable!functor categories Let $\calC $ be an presentable $\infty $-category, and let $K$ be a small simplicial set. Then $\Fun (K,\calC )$ is presentable. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      According to Proposition <a href="/tag/CBC4" data-tag="CBC4">5.4.4.3</a>, $\Fun (K,\calC )$ is accessible. It follows from Proposition <a href="/tag/4396" data-tag="4396">5.1.2.2</a> that if $\calC $ admits small colimits, then $\Fun (K,\calC )$ admits small colimits. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>